<p>Gig marketplaces are the easiest place to find your first clients; our <a href="/fiverr/">Fiverr guide</a> covers writing a gig that ranks. Online stores are a natural niche too, since every <a href="/shopify/">Shopify</a> merchant needs product and collection pages that rank. Price your packages with the <a href="/tools/freelance-rate-calculator/">freelance rate calculator</a> so platform fees and your subscription cost are covered.</p>

<div class="callout"><strong>Quick tip:</strong> A Semrush subscription is a business expense. Start with the free account or a trial while you learn, and upgrade once one or two clients cover the monthly cost.</div>

<h2 id="semrush-consultant">How to become a Semrush consultant</h2>
<p>"Semrush consultant" is not an official title, but clients search for it, and it signals that you can run the tool on their behalf. Here is a credible path:</p>
<ol class="steps">
  <li><strong>Take Semrush Academy courses.</strong> Semrush Academy offers free courses in SEO, content marketing, PPC and the tool itself. After a course you can take the certification exam and download a certificate at no cost.</li>
  <li><strong>Get certified on the tool.</strong> Tool-specific certifications are the most relevant proof for a client hiring a "Semrush expert." Add them to your profile and proposals.</li>
  <li><strong>Build case studies.</strong> Work on your own site or a friend's business for a few months. Before-and-after screenshots beat any certificate.</li>
  <li><strong>Pick a niche.</strong> "SEO for dentists" or "SEO for Shopify stores" is easier to sell, and to rank for, than generic SEO.</li>
  <li><strong>List yourself in Semrush Agency Partners.</strong> The Agency Partners directory lets agencies and consultants publish a profile that businesses browse when hiring. Semrush recommends Academy certification for a higher Agency Score; check the current requirements when you sign up.</li>
  <li><strong>Turn projects into retainers.</strong> Monthly reporting and content plans create steadier income than one-off audits.</li>
</ol>

